From: "mujiburrahimank@maxlinear.com"
 <mujiburrahimank@lvdocker7.lvsw.maxlinear.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 08:29:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] WLANRTSYS-102561 DFS switch channel on NOP-revert and trigger
 bgCAC when needed

Radar NOP-expiry revert path restored original chandef by disabling and enabling
the interface. This restart-based path is disruptive and can delay recovery.

Update revert handling to use DFS channel-switch flow and include background CAC
handling:

Keep original chandef restore logic on NOP completion.
Trigger DFS channel switch after restore instead of iface disable/enable.
Attempt background CAC for restored chandef when required/possible.
Fall back to DFS channel-switch path if bgCAC cannot be started.
Result:

Revert behavior is aligned with DFS channel-switch handling.
Reduces unnecessary interface restart during NOP recovery.
Preserves CAC requirements via bgCAC path where applicable.

Fixup to : WLANRTSYS-50839 MXL DFS debug channel simulation
---
